# Frontend

Generic frontend expectations. Stack wiring (Mantine, Tailwind, React Hook Form) lives in `stack/` — see `stack/react`, `stack/tailwind`, `stack/accessibility`.

## Forms

- Schema-driven validation; surface errors accessibly. Reuse the project's form stack rather than rolling your own.

## Accessibility

- Semantics first; ARIA only when HTML can't express intent. `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation, landmarks for structure. No `onClick` on a `<div>`.
- Keyboard path first: every interactive element reachable and operable. Manage `tabIndex` deliberately; restore focus on dialog close.
- Visible focus is non-negotiable: keep `:focus-visible`; never remove outlines globally.
- Label every control (`<label htmlFor>` or wrapping `<label>`); `aria-label` only for icon buttons.
- Announce dynamic state via `aria-live`/`aria-busy`.
- Don't rely on color alone — pair with text/icon. Meet WCAG AA contrast.
- Keep DOM order = visual order; restructure the DOM rather than reorder with CSS.
- `display:none`/`hidden` removes from the a11y tree; `sr-only` keeps it for AT. Pick deliberately.
